Package: singlet
Type: Package
Title: Single-Cell Genomics Toolkit
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zach", "DeBruine", email = "debruinz@gvsu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Read, write, and analyze single-cell data in the .1pz format.
    Provides zero-copy sparse matrix I/O with 13x compression, GPU-accelerated
    analysis (optional, requires CUDA 12+), and integration with
    SingleCellExperiment and Seurat objects. The .1pz codec is implemented in
    shared header-only C++ that is bit-identical to the Python package.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: false
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.10),
    Matrix (>= 1.5),
    methods
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp
Suggests:
    SingleCellExperiment,
    SummarizedExperiment,
    Seurat,
    BiocGenerics,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: C++17, libzstd (>= 1.4); optional: CUDA (>= 12.0)
Biarch: FALSE
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
